Why a separate licence. These source records quote the digitized Տօնացոյց
(Tonatsoyts, Jerusalem, 1915; the 1915 text is in the public domain) from the
grabar-ocr corpus: its Grabar transcription and its English machine
translation. That corpus is CC BY-NC 4.0 because its OCR was produced with
Calfa's models (hye-calfa-n, paddle-calfa-tiny; CC BY-NC 4.0), so material
quoting it carries the same terms. Grabar quotations are OCR by Calfa; English
quotations are machine translation by Google Gemini, not a human translation.

The armenian-lectionary package does not include this directory: the engine
cites the corpus by reference only and ships no corpus text.

When reusing this material, credit armenian-lectionary (Andy Litalo), the
grabar-ocr corpus, and Calfa for the OCR.
